ersion":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G7","usage":{"input_tokens":156790,"output_tokens":1847,"requests":3}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"9812051b249411eb51c3f570b1d506dff82704d27604ee7d9114ebe17876f879"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:T11","usage":{"input_tokens":192792,"output_tokens":4237,"requests":11}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"517eaba59dc99e0a2dafd8274aff901b3245d582a8125ce6885ce1eea474447d"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"single:COH,E1,E2,E6,F1,T2,T4,T5b,T5e,T7","usage":{"input_tokens":11981,"output_tokens":5535,"requests":1}},{"kind":"success","lineage":{"dependencies":[],"digest":"1de88de1a7807518b636569aa90861e015292cdc098fcef4f7992880c37dc593"},"namespace_version":1,"reason":null,"unit_id":"agent:G1G2","usage":{"input_tokens":896409,"output_tokens":9831,"requests":26}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Bump `_REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION` (8 → 9, comment naming RELEASE_DELTA / ADR 0124) in `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py`, and add that file to Scope.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.3,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py:29-31: 'Event metadata does not reflect changed projections. Including this manual version in the directory hash invalidates older caches. Increment it whenever projection semantics change.' / `_REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION = 8`","src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py:128: `hash_parts: list[str] = [f\"rv:{_REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION}\"]`; the rest of the hash is only event names, sizes, mtimes and the archived marker","The Scope list has no `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py` entry"],"finding":"The plan changes what the reducer computes (a new `releases` key in every compiled state, and a newly folded RELEASE_DELTA type) but does not bump `_REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION` in `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py`. That file is not in Scope. The cache key is only `rv:{_REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION}` plus event file names, sizes and mtimes, and the code comment says 'Increment it whenever projection semantics change.' Without a bump, the new binary serves states cached by the old binary: tickets with no new events come back with no `releases` key, and a ticket whose RELEASE_DELTA was folded (that is, ignored) by an older binary keeps returning stale state without the release names.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fb48dabc5068c1ca9","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Scope / Approach step 4 (Default); src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py:29-31","norm_id":"nd4c6faaf4aaa8ab3","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["After upgrading, `rebar show <tid>` on an untouched ticket returns a cached state with no `releases` key, even though `make_initial_state` now seeds `[]`.","A clone that reduced a ticket containing a RELEASE_DELTA file while on the old binary (unknown type, ignored) keeps serving the cached state without releases after upgrading, because the dir hash has not changed."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add an Approach step: in `src/rebar/reducer/_cache.py` set `_REDUCER_CACHE_VERSION = 9  # 9: releases field + RELEASE_DELTA fold (ADR 0124)`, and list the file under Scope.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add a reducer assertion that a TAG_DELTA leaves `releases == []`, and that the two lists are separate objects after both events fold.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.6062,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"extract the body of process_tag_delta into a private _fold_list_delta(state, key, data) and have both processors call it\"","AC: \"A RELEASE_DELTA never changes tags\" — there is no reverse criterion."],"finding":"The `_fold_list_delta(state, key, data)` extraction is pinned in only one direction. The no-leak test checks that RELEASE_DELTA leaves `tags` alone, but nothing checks that TAG_DELTA leaves `releases` alone. The unchanged tag tests do not inspect `releases`.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f46656434b62194e6","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 2 (shared fold); Testing 'a RELEASE_DELTA leaves tags unchanged'","norm_id":"n1a8bcf49f6f361a7","priority":0.3438,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A wrong `key` argument or a shared-default mutation in the helper makes TAG_DELTA also write `releases`, and every planned test still passes."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In test_reducer_release_delta.py, reduce [CREATE, TAG_DELTA{added:['x']}] and assert state['releases'] == []; then add a RELEASE_DELTA and assert state['tags'] is not state['releases'].","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Name `src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_receipt.py` / `ticket_view.receipt()` as consumers of the SCHEMA_VERSION bump, and state (in the plan and in the v6 history entry) that receipts stamped `reducer_schema_version` 5 are rejected after upgrade and how in-flight bases are handled.","cohort":["G1G2"],"criteria":["G1G2"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.425,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_view.py:404-409: `\"reducer_schema_version\": SCHEMA_VERSION` in the receipt","src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_receipt.py:78-85: `receipt.get(\"reducer_schema_version\") == SCHEMA_VERSION`","src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_receipt.py:144-145,175-176: `raise ValueError(\"unsupported ticket read receipt schema\")`","The plan says the bump is for older clones to 'preserve and ignore'; it never mentions read receipts"],"finding":"Bumping `SCHEMA_VERSION` 5→6 affects a consumer the plan does not mention: durable ticket read receipts. `ticket_view.receipt()` stamps `reducer_schema_version: SCHEMA_VERSION`, and `ticket_receipt._receipt_schema_matches` requires it to equal the current SCHEMA_VERSION. `CompletionReadBasis.__post_init__` and `from_dict` raise `ValueError('unsupported ticket read receipt schema')` on a mismatch. Any completion read basis or receipt persisted under v5 becomes unparseable after this change. The plan's Context and the v6 doc entry describe the bump only as an event-log forward-compat marker.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5f81939e11fd5cb1","impact":0.44,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 1 (SCHEMA_VERSION bump) / step 8 (v6 history entry); src/rebar/_snapshot/ticket_receipt.py:78-85,144,175,292","norm_id":"nac07c59e900c24b8","priority":0.275,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A completion-verification run that saved a `completion_read_basis_v1` before the upgrade fails to reload it afterwards, because `from_dict` raises ValueError."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.625,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"incomplete_enumeration","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State in step 6/8 how compaction on a pre-v6 clone treats unknown RELEASE_DELTA events (kept after the SNAPSHOT, or compaction refused by SCHEMA_VERSION), and add a store test or cite the existing guard that pins it.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["T4","T5b"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"a new event body type, so older clones preserve and ignore it, and the reconcile host is upgraded first\"","\"compaction stores the reduced state as SNAPSHOT.compiled_state\" — reduced by whichever clone runs compaction","The plan names no mechanism (such as unknown-type events kept after the snapshot, or a SCHEMA_VERSION gate on compaction) that keeps a downgraded clone from erasing releases."],"finding":"The plan does not say what happens when an OLDER clone, which ignores RELEASE_DELTA, compacts a ticket whose log already contains RELEASE_DELTA events. That clone's SNAPSHOT.compiled_state would have no `releases` key. If compaction drops or archives the folded pre-snapshot events, the release data is lost. 'Older clones preserve and ignore it' covers replay, not compaction.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f5061b1df1cc5f623","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 6 (Snapshot) and step 8 (Docs, v6 forward-compat entry)","norm_id":"n21d436fe869e6308","priority":0.0,"reason":"veto:cited-reference-inaccurate","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A teammate on a pre-v6 rebar runs `rebar store compact` after the inbound sync child has written RELEASE_DELTA events; the next show_ticket on a v6 clone returns `releases == []`."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"no","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Extend the pre-feature snapshot test to also assert that a log of only the pre-feature SNAPSHOT reduces to `releases == []`.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E6","E1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.7929,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC: \"A pre-feature snapshot replays to `[]` and then accepts later deltas\"","Test: \"a pre-feature `SNAPSHOT` (no `releases` key) followed by a `RELEASE_DELTA` yields the delta's names\""],"finding":"The pre-feature-snapshot criterion claims two things: the snapshot replays to `[]`, and it then accepts deltas. The planned test only checks the state after a following RELEASE_DELTA, so the `[]` intermediate state is never asserted.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f50a5148b588c5fa2"